  "result": "I added `split(cents, parts)` to `shop/money.py` and a new test file, `tests/test_money.py`. All 12 tests pass, the 6 new ones included.\n\n- **How it works:** it uses `divmod` to get the base amount and the leftover cents. The first `remainder` elements each get one extra cent, so `split(100, 3)` gives `[34, 33, 33]`. If `parts` is below 1, it raises `ValueError`.\n- **What the tests check:**\n  - an even split\n  - the leftover cents going to the first elements\n  - fewer cents than parts (`split(2, 4)` gives `[1, 1, 0, 0]`)\n  - a single part\n  - the results always summing to `cents` and having length `parts`, over a range of inputs\n  - `ValueError` for `parts` of 0 and -1\n\nI didn't test negative `cents`. The results still add up to the right total, but larger amounts come last, not first: `split(-5, 2)` gives `[-2, -3]`. If negative amounts will be passed in, you may want to decide which order you want.",
